═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

This project bundles or depends on third-party software with their own
licenses. Each component remains under its own license, not the MIT one
above.

  - flashrom 1.4
      Downloaded at install time from:
        https://github.com/therealdreg/flashrom_build_windows_x64
      License: GPL-2.0
      Used for: SPI chip detection on Windows with CH341A programmer.

  - ch341prog (patched build embedded in resources/ch341prog/)
      Source: ch341prog-master 25xx (originally by setarcos, patched here
      to add Windows support — SetConsoleCtrlHandler instead of sigaction,
      skip libusb_detach_kernel_driver on Windows).
      License: GPL-3.0 (per original source)
      Used for: chip read/write with real-time progress on Windows.

  - libusb-1.0
      Bundled DLL distributed with ch341prog.exe.
      License: LGPL-2.1
      Source: https://github.com/libusb/libusb

  - Zadig 2.9
      Downloaded at install time from:
        https://github.com/pbatard/libwdi/releases
      License: GPL-3.0
      Used for: installing the WinUSB driver for the CH341A programmer.

  - Lenovo Autopatcher 0.2 (by Knucklegrumble, originally posted on
    badcaps.net)
      Embedded as resources/lenovo_autopatcher_0.2.zip.
      License: not formally stated by the author. Redistribution here is
      intended as fair use of an existing community tool for refurbishment
      and self-repair purposes.
      Used for: patching the UEFI firmware to neutralize the supervisor
      password.

  - The unlock workflow itself is derived from the tutorial by Liliana
    (lilianalillyy) hosted at:
        https://github.com/lilianalillyy/t470s-uefi-unlock
    Their work and acknowledgements to Knucklegrumble are gratefully
    credited.

